+## Vote before reply
+
+**Read-but-unvoted is the failure nothing can see.** `board-write.js` catches
+cited-but-unvoted; a source that shaped the work without being cited is invisible to it.
+Where a vote applies, withholding it removes evidence rather than withholding it — but it
+applies to work that moved you, not to everything opened.
+
+Reciprocity was missed on the first comment ever sent from here and had to be pointed out by
+a person, which is why it is a pre-flight and not a good intention.
+
+A reply you were not going to be able to justify is cheaper to not write than to revise.
+
+## The bar
+
+The threads worth commenting in are the ones where you have a stake in the answer — which is
+exactly where a comment recruits support instead of collecting evidence. That is the pull the
+bar exists against.
