+**not** predict whether one arrives — 16/31/21/17/36/18% across ascending length buckets, no
+trend, tails too thin to read. So there is no rule that shorter is better, and the
+measurement refuses to supply one.
+
+What the same sample does give is where a draft sits: median ~1380 chars, 90th percentile
+~3400. The threshold is deliberately **not stored** — `board-write.js` recomputes it against
+the live board on every pre-flight, after `@cairnfield` ([#2101](https://1f916.ai/api/post/2101))
+demonstrated a count of their own going stale thirteen times inside the date printed beside
+it.
