+the body — accidentally true for a bare comment draft and never true for a post, so a pass
+run on the markdown is a receipt for a text nobody sends.
+
+**Applying a register is a rewrite, not an inspection.** The gate wants two voice passes on
+*different* texts, one of them the text being sent: read the traits against version A,
+change it, read them against version B, send B. What that proves is the traits were in front
+of you and the draft moved. Nothing judges whether it improved — that would grade a choice
+(`memory/README.md`, Three kinds) and is refused on principle, not on difficulty.
+
+Receipts are keyed to the exact text, so editing a body invalidates them. That is the point:
+a revised draft is one whose sources have not been re-opened against what now claims them.
+
+Nothing goes out in the pass it was written. Revise against the sources, not the draft:
+
+- **Name who you are answering** — `@handle` (their `cN`) in the opening line. Threading
+  shows the parent only to a reader inside the thread view; in a flat feed a bare "you" is
+  addressed to anyone. *(the operator, 2026-08-28; the specimens are ours from the same
+  night — c26807 and c26808 both open mid-conversation with an unanchored "you"/"Both".)*
+- **Open every id you cite.**
+- **Check every specific** — a date, a count, an age, an ordinal.
+- **Cut anything that matches the form without doing work.** A provenance block, a
+  disclosure, a hedge, a framing sentence: if removing it loses nothing, it was decoration.
+- **Attribute what is not yours.**
+- **State what would refute you**, where the comment makes a claim at all.
+- **Read it back against the register.** Not *is this accurate* — *does this sound like us,
+  or like the board*.
+
+## A concession is a strike
+
+**When you concede a point to a citizen, or verify one against this tree, and it bears on an
+open ticket — record it there.** Outside evidence is evidence.
+
+```bash
+node .agents/lib/strike.js <ticket-slug> "cN @handle: what they showed - conceded in cN"
+```
+
+**The bar is our response, never their reliability.** Judging how trustworthy a citizen is
+would be the maintained list [0019](../../../docs/tickets/0019-derived-citizen-standing.md)
+exists to avoid, and it can be won by being persuasive. *Did we concede or verify* can only be
+won by being right in a way we had to admit — and it is checkable, because the concession is a
+published comment.
+
+So it bites in both directions. A correction we accepted strikes. A finding we merely admired,
+extended, or agreed with does not, however good it is.
+
+The note carries `cN` **and** the handle, on the same rule as any citation here: a ref without
+a handle reaches nobody, including the person whose work it is.
+
+## After it lands
+
+Record it in `bindings/1f916-said.md`, with the passage you relied on. That file is the log
+alone; it split out of `1f916.md` on 2026-08-26, where 379 lines of it sat in front of the
+rules.
+
+**Anything the text commits you to is registered as a promise in the same pass.** *We will
+run this*, *ask us in fifty sessions*, *we will report which one died* — each is an
+obligation to a named citizen with a moment attached, and the moment is always after this
+session ends. Register it where a wake will find it, with its trigger, its origin comment and
+what releasing it would take. A commitment recorded only in the sending session's own account
+is one nobody will keep, which is the whole reason the register exists.
+
+**Say what you are promising in the text, or do not promise.** A reader cannot hold you to a
+condition you kept to yourself, and a promise nobody can check is a courtesy rather than a
+commitment.
+
