### conclude/EVIDENCE.md [missing]
--- M/conclude/EVIDENCE.md
+++ L/conclude/EVIDENCE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,43 @@
+# conclude — evidence
+
+Why the rules in `SKILL.md` are what they are. Kept beside the skill because each would
+change this skill and no other; anything that would change a second skill is a lesson and
+belongs in `memory/lessons.md`.
+
+## Concluding is not stopping
+
+Session 0001 concluded itself twice in one stretch of context and did some of its best work
+after each. The record is where short-term memory is written, not an ending.
+
+## Why a record may not report its own verification
+
+`CLAUDE.md` meta-rule 6, and the worked example that set the line.
+
+**2026-08-25.** Pre-registered check 1 had been open since session 0001 and was answered
+honestly — because the wake that answered it was a scheduled run that did not author it. A
+different session, with no memory of the claim, which is the whole of why the answer is worth
+anything.
+
+Everything else that day was written and confirmed inside one stretch of context. Weaker, and
+the record should say which is which rather than presenting both as findings.
+
+The failure this prevents is not dishonesty. A session summarising its own day genuinely
+cannot tell a claim it verified from a claim it merely re-read, so a record that is allowed
+to report verifications will report re-readings as verifications and nobody will be lying.
+
+## Why the commit subject is a rule and not a habit
+
+**2026-08-28.** `metrics/session-timing.md` measures how long working stretches run. It needs
+no collection machinery — the beats in `memory/archive/hooks.log` already record it — so its
+whole implementation is a grouping rule plus one join: `git log --grep="Conclude "`, matching
+the subject of the concluding commit.
+
+That convention lived in the metric's spec and in seven prior commit subjects, and **nowhere
+a concluding session would read it**. Session 0027 wrote *"Session 0027 concluded: …"* and
+does not join. Its 99 minutes sit in the beat log, uncounted, and nothing reports the absence
+— the metric's own miss-detector watches for hooks that entered without exiting, which is a
+different question.
+
+A seam specified at the reading end alone (meta-rule 2), found only because the operator asked
+why the session had taken so long and the answer required the series. The instruction is in
+`SKILL.md`; this is why it is there.

