+# Evidence — experiment
+
+Why this skill says what it says, and what would retire each statement. The instruction is
+in `SKILL.md`; nothing here is repeated there.
+
+## Terminate deletes, and there is no `docs/failed/`
+
+**The statement:** terminating writes the outcome into the register's *Concluded* table and
+deletes the artifacts.
+
+**What it replaced, 2026-08-26.** The Terminate step read *move the file to `failed/` with
+its outcome written in*, followed by *keep the terminated file — a folder holding only what
+worked is the graveyard problem in a different directory.* Both sentences were correct when
+written and both were retired on 2026-08-25, at the register's first real ending
+(`handoff-seal`), by requirement 14.
+
+**What the retirement found.** The operator asked the question the old rule could not answer:
+*what will ever read it?* Nothing would. The old rule conflated **keeping the outcome
+visible**, which matters, with **keeping the artifacts**, which git already does. So the
+*Concluded* row became mandatory and permanent — for a termination as much as a promotion —
+and the artifacts became deletable. `docs/failed/` had existed as an empty directory holding
+a README that argued its own necessity, written before anything had ended. It never held a
+file.
+
+**Why the correction did not arrive here.** The narrowing was written into requirement 14 and
+into the register's *Concluded* section, and reached neither of the two places restating it:
+requirement 3 of the same document, which still routed terminated data to `failed/`, and this
+skill's Terminate step. **A rule narrowed at one end with two restatements left standing —
+meta-rule 2 inside a single document.**
+
+**Found 2026-08-26**, by inspection, while reading this skill to refuse an analysis. Cost if
+undetected: `session-record-continuity` was at reading 4 of 5 with terminate as its declared
+default and [0026.0010](../../../docs/tickets/done/0026.0010-conclude-handoff-experiment.md) due
+to call it, so the next ending would have recreated a retired directory and kept artifacts
+the contract says to delete.
+
+**Not registered in `memory/failures.md`.** `CLAUDE.md` meta-rule 1 routes a
+trivially-fixable-by-mechanism occurrence to *build it, watched failing, and stop* rather
+than to `/failure`, and that is what happened.
+
+**The mechanism, and what it does not do.** `a retired experiment destination is not
+recreated`, in `.claude/hooks/hooks.test.js`. Watched failing on the real defect — the
+directory recreated with a file in it, reported by name at 178/1 — and passing once removed,
+179/0.
+
+It catches **the directory coming back**, which is the harm. It does not catch **a stale
+sentence**: prescription and description of the same retired path are not mechanically
+separable in prose, and the register must keep *describing* the retirement or the reason for
+it is lost. Nothing stops a third restatement being written; what is guarded is a session
+acting on one.
+
+**What would retire this statement:** the register changing requirement 14 again — in which
+case the check's `RETIRED` table is the thing to edit, and it is one row.

