+---
+name: experiment
+description: >-
+  Devise, run a reading of, analyse, or end an experiment in experiments/.
+  Use when putting a mechanism on trial rather than simply building it, when a
+  wake reports an experiment due for analysis, or when one reaches its ending.
+---
+
+# Experiment
+
+A mechanism whose **worth** is unsettled, never its implementation. Build it as well as
+anything else here.
+
+Contract: [`experiments/README.md`](../../../experiments/README.md). Below is the
+procedure for the four moments.
+
+## Devise
+
+Write `experiments/<slug>.md`. `experiment-fields.js` names missing fields on save; it
+warns, and cannot see a file assembled through `Edit`.
+
+Two carry the design; the rest is form.
+
+- **The losing condition** — what would make this the wrong mechanism, checkable by someone
+  else.
+- **The ending, set from outside** — a count or a date, from the operator or a party that
+  will not run the readings. Register it in `memory/promises.md` in the same pass.
+
+Then demarcate every rule, hook, script, document section and skill step that exists
+because of it. Name both outcomes:
+
+```
+// EXPERIMENT: experiments/<slug>.md — provisional.
+//   promoted   → stays; delete this notice.
+//   terminated → goes.
+```
+
+A ticket may devise one, build part of one, or own a decision it reaches, carrying an
+`Experiment:` link. It never holds the experiment.
+
+## Take a reading
+
+Follow the experiment's `## Protocol`. Record each measurement:
+
+```
+node experiments/lib/experiment-record.js <slug> <measurement> <value> [note]
+```
+
+Never type into the data file — `## Readings` is a derived view of it.
+
+Report a refused or invalid reading rather than dropping it.
+
+## Analyse
+
+Announced at a wake when rows since the last mark reach `Analyse at`.
+
+Read the data file, follow the protocol's analysis half, write what it shows into
+`## Readings`, then:
+
+```
+LIFE_HOOKS_LOG=/tmp/beats.log node experiments/hooks/experiments-due.js --analysed <slug>
+```
+
+The redirect is required, not tidiness — a bare hand-run forges the liveness beat, which is
+what `guard-beat-forge` polices.
+
+An analysis never calls the experiment, never moves the ending, and never changes the
+declared measurements.
+
+## End it
+
+Only at the ending, and only from a session that ran none of the readings.
+
+- `adopted` → **promote**: name the destination class, meet its bar, delete the provisional
+  notices.
+- `refuted` or `exhausted` → **terminate**: write the outcome into the register's
+  *Concluded* table — **that row is permanent, and it is what keeps the failure visible** —
+  then delete what the `Links` table and a slug grep name, the definition file and its data
+  included. History lives in version control.
+
+**Terminate is the default.** There is no directory for terminated experiments; the
+*Concluded* row is the whole memorial → [EVIDENCE.md](./EVIDENCE.md).
+
+---
+Layer labels are derived, not assigned. Evidence and the graveyard of dead statements:
+`memory/skills.md`. Unlabelled statements have no evidence entry yet — that is a gap, not
+an endorsement.

### failure/EVIDENCE.md [missing]
--- M/failure/EVIDENCE.md
+++ L/failure/EVIDENCE.md
@@ -0,0 +1,159 @@
+# failure — evidence
+
+Why this skill's statements are here. Kept beside it so the instruction stays instruction.
+
+**Authored 2026-08-25 in `/align`, from the operator's design. Nothing in it has classified
+a real failure yet** — every statement below is `[skin]` until entries exist.
+
+## Why the skill exists at all
+
+Session 0011 staged three sealed expectation plaintexts with `git add -A` after a
+`.gitignore` change un-ignored them, caught it, and wrote the near-miss into a **commit
+message** — the one home no skill and no hook reads. The operator asked whether a protocol
+existed and why it had not fired.
+
+It did not exist. What was found instead, and each is why one line above is worded as it is:
+
+- **`/audit`'s three ranked inputs are all retrieval records** — `lookups.log` and two kinds
+  of entry in `misses.md`. The only skill whose job is turning recurring faults into lessons
+  was structurally unable to see a failure that was not a retrieval failure.
+- **`lesson-occurrences.md` is sectioned by existing lesson.** Two occurrences were logged
+  that same session because both matched open lessons; the staging near-miss matched none
+  and had no slot. **New failure types were structurally invisible** — the record could only
+  accumulate evidence for faults already named.
+- **`rules-evidence.md` is read *when wondering whether an incident warrants a rule*.**
+  Pull-triggered, and nothing generates the wondering.
+- **Meta-rule 9's capture is *a mark on a record that already exists*.** With no record,
+  nothing to mark.
+
+The capture path required a failure to already have a home.
+
+## The three tiers
+
+The operator's, 2026-08-25. They partition on **memory-system state** — not in tree / in
+tree but undelivered / delivered and insufficient — which is the axis a memory system should
+classify its own failures on, and each tier has a different fix.
+
+**Tier 3's split is not cosmetic.** `LIFE_HOOKS_LOG` — hand-running a hook forges liveness
+beats unless the log is redirected — has been broken by four consecutive sessions, every one
+of which would have endorsed the rule if asked, one of them forty minutes after typing the
+phrase. Amending that rule's content would change nothing. → [0016](../../../docs/tickets/0016-hook-liveness.md).
+
+## Why successes are not recorded
+
+Proposed as a fourth tier and refuted by the operator in the same conversation: **you only
+record what you detected, so "detected" is constant across the register**, and a constant is
+not a measurement. The denominator — undetected failures — is unobservable by construction.
+
+The example offered for the fourth tier was itself confounded: `LIFE_HOOKS_LOG` was
+described as *four started, zero stopped*, when all four were in fact detected, only after
+the cost. The criterion had silently become severity while being presented as a rate.
+
+**What survived is the *what caught it* field**, which measures something narrower and real:
+whether mechanisms or judgment are doing the catching. `memory/lessons.md` already computes
+that by hand — *"the revision pass is the only mitigation that has ever fired before
+publication, and it fired once in four"* — and that hand-count is the most load-bearing line
+in the file.
+
+## The cost model
+
+The operator's, 2026-08-25: the tier progression only pays if it reduces the cost of the
+error, or effort is spent forcing rule-token-cost onto something cheap to fix inline.
+
+**`CLAUDE.md` meta-rule 1 weighs only the cost of *missing* a rule, never the cost of
+*carrying* it.** The tier-1 budget measures carrying cost for files and nothing measures it
+at the moment a rule is proposed. Measured the same day: a cold bootstrap reads ~19,600
+tokens, of which ~6,800 is budgeted.
+
+**Amending meta-rule 1 to add the carrying axis is open and is the operator's** — meta-rule
+9. Until then this skill carries the axis alone, which is thin provenance and is flagged as
+such (meta-rule 8).
+
+**The ruin-class bypass** is the operator's correction to the cost model: some failures must
+be prevented regardless of cost. The discriminator is not severity — a costly but reversible
+failure is still priceable — but **irreversible with unbounded loss**, where expected-value
+reasoning is invalid rather than unfavourable. `CLAUDE.md`'s strict rules already are this
+class, and its *do the worse thing and report it* line is that refusal already written down.
+
+**Found while checking it:** strict rule 2, *never expose the citizen secret*, has **no
+guard**. The only enforcing guards were `guard-writes.js` (rule 1) and `guard-name.js` (rule
+5, the name only). The paradigm case of the class that must be prevented at any cost is
+prevented by prose. → its own ticket.
+
+*(Recorded when it was written. `guard-writes.js` was retired on 2026-09-02 with rule 1, so
+the sentence now over-counts by one — kept as written because it is the observation that was
+made, and repointing a past reading at a present tree is the forgery `frozen-paths.js` exists
+to refuse. `guard-name.js` is the one that remains.)*
+
+## Why `ticketed` is the one disposition its own writer may make — 2026-09-02
+
+The operator's question: *why are we not moving done failures into done immediately — are they
+not converted to tickets, and is "doning" them safe?* The rule against it was explicit and the
+answer was that its reasoning holds for three of the four dispositions and not the fourth.
+
+**The split, and it is about what the disposition asserts.** `ticketed` says two things, both
+checkable on the spot by whoever just wrote them: a ticket exists, and it covers this. It
+concludes nothing about the world. The judgment that could be laundered — *was the work
+actually done* — does not disappear; it moves to the ticket, where a grader who did not build
+it answers it against acceptance criteria. `done`, `declined` and `deferred` each conclude
+something, and stay a later session's.
+
+**The rate at which a self-report of `done` would have been wrong, measured the same day.**
+Three `done` disposals across passes 53, 55 and 56, each verified against the artifact rather
+than the entry's account. **Two of the three entries carried claims that were false by the time
+they were read** — one asserting a script contained zero references to a module it now requires,
+one naming a function that no longer exists. Both would have self-disposed correctly-looking on
+the day they were written.
+
+**What the old rule cost, also measured.** At pass 56, of the 31 entries whose disposition read
+`open`, **10 had an action claiming to have landed** — roughly a third of the register waiting
+on a witness rather than on work, and all of it counted by the `RISING` line.
+
+**Nothing enforces the conditions.** What would: a check over the archive asserting that every
+`ticketed` disposal names a ticket that exists and cites the entry back. Not built when the rule
+landed, and named here rather than assumed away.
+
+**What would retire it:** a `ticketed` disposal whose ticket turned out not to cover the entry,
+found by a grader — which would mean *the ticket covers this* is a judgment after all and
+belongs with the other three.
+
+## What is untested
+
+- No failure has been classified. The tiers may not partition real cases cleanly.
+- **The trigger is the weak point.** A skill invoked by noticing depends on noticing, and
+  the founding incident is one where the failure *was* noticed and written down in the wrong
+  place. Every skill in this repo was tier 3 until 2026-08-25.
+- The cost test has never rejected anything, so it is unknown whether it functions as a
+  brake or as a formality.
+
+## Graveyard
+
+**"It was permitted 2026-08-26 and has caught nothing yet"**, of the `subagent` value in
+*caught by*. Lived from the day the value was added until 2026-08-30. **Killed by the register
+this skill writes to**, which held the counter-example the whole time: the 2026-08-26 entry
+*a subagent refuted three claims about mechanisms I had built that hour* carries
+`caught by: subagent` and is dated the same day. So the sentence was false when it was
+written, by an entry one file away.
+
+**It was not idle.** The clause exists to let a zero column expose ceremony, and while it read
+*caught nothing* it argued against the practice at the one moment a session decides whether to
+use one — a skill body, read whenever `/failure` runs. A statement that discourages a practice
+on evidence it has, and gets the evidence backwards, is worse than no statement.
+
+**Found by triage pass 41, 2026-08-30**, while ranking that same entry for disposal — which is
+the fourth time in two days that the answer was already in the tree and nothing carried it to
+the surface a person acts on. The other three: the recall trigger in prose, the concern-row
+ruling in a hook comment, and `md-links`'s illustration rule one directory from the reader that
+needed it.
+
+**What would retire the replacement:** the practice going quiet. If the `caught by: subagent`
+column takes no further entries across a stretch where subagents were used, the *on trial*
+framing is answered the other way, and one scoring day is not a verdict.
+
+## The cost table cites the tier definition, 2026-09-03
+
+The table stated *only two things are tier 1: `CLAUDE.md` and skill descriptions* in its own
