+# implement — what licensed it
+
+## What it replaced, and why the replacement is a rewrite
+
+Until 2026-09-02 this file held the reference corpus's software-delivery skill, verbatim and
+unported. What it asked for, in its own words: *use very slight alchemical cyber/steampunk
+laboratory inclination when picking names*, *use `/tdd` where possible*, *once done, use
+`/sync-arch` to review the work*, and *do not commit your work until requested*.
+
+Three of those could not be followed here and one was forbidden:
+
+- **`/tdd` does not exist in this tree.** A skill routing to a skill that is not present is
+  the reachability defect `skills-reachable.js` was built for, sitting inside the skill set.
+- **`/sync-arch` is itself unadapted** — zero project references in its body — so the review
+  step routed to a second unported skill.
+- **The architecture vocabulary was a different domain's.** *Boundaries*, *contract surfaces*,
+  *client-oriented naming*: correct where it came from, and this tree's work is hooks,
+  registers and records.
+- **"Do not commit your work until requested" contradicted a standing operator instruction**
+  (2026-08-25, *commit without asking*) and `/commit`, which owns the judgment. Porting the
+  file as it stood would have imported a rule that loses to a strict-rule-adjacent one.
+
+So the port was never a port. That is why it sat unported for six days while
+`core/process.md` stage 4 kept naming it.
+
+## The measurement that forced the rewrite
+
+The operator asked, 2026-09-02, whether a skill that resolves tickets exists. Counted the same
+hour:
+
+| | |
+|---|---|
+| open tickets | 95 |
+| carrying a `Mechanism` field | 42 |
+| carrying none | **53** |
+| session records naming `/align` | 31 |
+| naming `/mechanism` | 30 |
+| naming `/maintain` | 11 |
+| naming `/ticket` | 6 |
+| naming `/implement`, `/plan-impl`, `/sync-arch`, `/tdd` | **0 each** |
+
+Fifty-three tickets with no adapted owner, and the loop routing all of them to a file nobody
+had ever opened for work. `/triage`'s routing sentence had been amended an hour earlier to
+require a named owner per pick, and its own retire condition fired immediately on this gap —
+that exchange is in `triage/EVIDENCE.md` and `C38`.
+
+## Why the boundary question is first, and why it is expected to say "mechanism"
+
+`CLAUDE.md` meta-rule 10 requires `/mechanism` **before** building or amending one, so a build
+that discovers its subject was a mechanism has already broken a rule that cannot be repaired
+afterwards. Putting the question anywhere but first makes the breach undetectable from the
+artifact.
+
+The 42-of-95 count predicts this skill hands work away more often than it keeps it. That is
+stated in the body so a session does not read a referral as this skill failing to apply.
+
+## What is deliberately not here
+
+- **Grading.** Owned by `/ticket`'s `TICKET-FORMAT.md`, *Grading — the act*. Restating it
+  would put the same rule in two homes (meta-rule 7), and the half that matters here — a
+  builder never ticks — is one sentence with a pointer.
+- **Both polarities.** Meta-rule 3 already says it. What this skill adds is the *moment*:
+  the defect is reproducible during the build and not afterwards.
+- **Planning.** `/plan-impl` is the reference corpus's and is also unported. Whether it earns
+  an adaptation is a separate question and no session has ever named it either.
+- **A test-driven-development instruction.** The tree has one suite and meta-rule 3; a second
+  vocabulary for the same discipline would be a competing home.
+
+## What would retire the statements
+
+- **The boundary question first** — a build where asking it first cost something and asking it
+  at the end would have cost nothing, which would mean the ordering is ceremony.
+- **The criteria are the contract** — a ticket whose criteria were unreadable before the work
+  because the work is what revealed them, which is the case for a criterion that could only be
+  written afterwards.
+- **A wrong criterion is struck before the work lands** — a builder who does this and a grader
+  who then finds the restatement was self-serving, which would mean the move needs the grader
+  after all.
+- **The whole skill** — every open ticket acquiring a `Mechanism` field, which would mean
+  `/mechanism` covers the class and this one has no subject.

