+# Mechanism
+
+**Incept** builds something others will rely on. **Amend** returns to one already standing —
+its shape moved, or you want to know whether it still holds — and re-checks everything
+relying on it.
+
+Not how to write code. The conventions that outlive whoever ran it. Why any of it:
+[EVIDENCE.md](./EVIDENCE.md).
+
+## What counts
+
+**Does something else rely on this as a source of instructions or behaviour?** Reliance, not
+code. A rule nobody is routed to fails the test. A directory layout three programs read
+passes it.
+
+**A system, never a file** — one spans a hook, a skill, a library, a register, a wake line.
+
+**Records sit inside mechanisms**: a register is the third shape and its readers are parts.
+Writing an *entry* is not mechanism work — that belongs to the skill owning the entry `[E10]`.
+
+## The three shapes `[bone]`
+
+Meta-rule 10 routes here and states none of this; **this is its only home.**
+
+| shape | holds | read when | story |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| **doc** | what it **is** and what it is **for**; how it works, install/uninstall, **its moments**, **every rule it injects and where**, and **it names the instruction files** | installing, removing, amending, debugging — never in ordinary work | **no** |
+| **instruction file** | the rules that get injected. Current state only. **Usually a skill, and there may be several** | in the work it governs | **no** |
+| **sidecars** | history and data | when the trace is the question | yes |
+
+**Only the sidecar takes story.** A doc excludes why the shape is this, what it cost, what was
+refuted, what it used to be, and when each changed — **one sidecar for all of it** *(the
+operator, 2026-08-30)*, `<slug>.evidence.md`. Decisions a person made stay in the owning
+ticket's `## Resolutions`.
+
+**Doc and instruction file are never the same file** (the operator, 2026-08-27) — checked by
+`mechanisms-shape.js`. Whether they may share a **sidecar** is open and the operator's.
+
+### Injection and retraction `[bone]`
+
+**A mechanism does not always get its own instruction file. It injects rules into skills that
+already exist** *(the operator, 2026-08-28)*. M08 and M12 have named two instruction surfaces
+each since before this was written down — the practice preceded the rule.
+
+- **The rules live in `mechanisms/<slug>/<slug>.rules.md`, one demarcated section per rule,
+  each naming its own target** *(the operator, 2026-08-28)*. That file is their only home.
+  A copy in a target is installed, never authored.
+- **The injector is generic**: `.agents/scripts/inject-rules.js <slug>`. One script for every
+  mechanism — per-mechanism installers holding rule text is the shape this replaced, and it
+  put the rules in two places while this page asserted the wrong one.
+- **Injection is mechanical in both directions or it is not injection.** A rule added by hand
+  is retracted by whoever remembers it, which is nobody.
+- **Retraction removes the clause and never the host.** The skill it was injected into
+  pre-existed the mechanism and outlives it.
+- **Of the two retractions, `<slug>.uninstall.js` defaults to pause and disable is asked for**
+  *(the operator, 2026-08-28)*. A retraction whose bare invocation destroys data is one someone
+  runs once by accident. **The scope is the uninstaller and only the uninstaller** *(the
+  operator, 2026-08-29)* — this sentence stood unscoped here, `inject-rules.js` implemented it
+  as its own default across install and retract alike, and a bare invocation therefore
+  retracted. **`inject-rules.js` has no default mode and names one or refuses.**
+
+**Turning a mechanism off is two different acts, and the difference is the data**
+*(the operator, 2026-08-28)*. Both retract every injected rule and unregister every hook;
+**neither deletes the definition, ever.**
+
+| act | injected rules | hooks | accumulated data | the definition |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| **pause** / **stop** | retracted | unregistered | **kept** | stays in `mechanisms/<slug>/` |
+| **disable** | retracted | unregistered | **deleted** | **folded into a separate folder, never deleted** |
+
+**Pause is for a mechanism that will run again** — its series continues where it stopped, and
+a gap in the data is a fact about the pause rather than a hole. **Disable is for one that has
+finished**: nothing will read its rows again, which is the question that decides between them.
+
+**The doc keeps every injected rule while the mechanism is off**, in both acts. That is what
+makes turning it back on mechanical rather than a reconstruction, and it is why the register
+row and the doc survive a disable that removes everything else.
+
+Anything that *truly* leaves the tree is `/denoise`'s and `/triage`'s to decide, never a side
+effect of either act.
+
+**Deleting the data and deleting the definition were one act until this split.** They are not
+the same question: nothing reads a dead mechanism's rows, and the definition is the only thing
+that says what it was and what it decided. Disable answers both correctly and neither did
+before.
+
+**A mechanism may spawn promises** *(the operator, 2026-08-28)*. An obligation with a moment
+after this session belongs in `memory/promises.md` where a wake will find it, carrying the
+mechanism's slug; uninstalling releases them in writing rather than dropping them.
+
