+**A backlog is a ratchet, never a threshold.** Where a mechanism ships with a standing
+backlog, count it and hold the count: silent at or below the mark, loud when it **rises**. A
+mark is **lowered** freely as the backlog clears — that is what progress looks like — and
+**raised only by a stated change of definition, with the cause written beside the number.** A
+re-baseline and the drift the mark exists to catch are otherwise indistinguishable. A hook
+that announces a standing backlog every wake is noise, and noise is what gets routed around.
+
