+## Incept
+
+1. **Name the seam and both ends before writing either.** Who produces, who consumes, how a
+   mismatch shows. The consuming end is what goes missing, because building the producer
+   feels like the work. *Someone will look* is not a reader.
+2. **Expand the shape first** — instances, polarities, quantities, kind; then where it lives
+   and who consumes it. Enumerate what is there, not what the shape implies. Where expansion
+   is expensive, say it was skipped.
+3. **Align before building.** `/align`, every incepted mechanism, no exceptions — and open it
+   by **explaining what the mechanism is** in plain terms. A mechanism nobody can describe is
+   one whose doc will describe the wrong thing. *(the operator, 2026-08-27)*
+4. **Assign the layer before the file exists**, or it gets decided by where the file landed.
+5. **Watch it fail.** Real defect, both polarities, at authoring time. A check never watched
+   failing is not a check, and it is believed harder than the note it replaced.
+6. **Run it over what already exists.** From landing it sees only new writes; every prior
+   violation is invisible to it forever. Fix what it finds, or **record the count** —
+   *nothing has tripped it since* means nothing while the backlog is unmeasured.
+7. **Produce the shape, not just the working part.** Steps 1–6 build a part and stop; that is
+   how two mechanisms were incepted in one day with no directory and no scripts. Not incepted
+   until it has: **a directory**, **a doc** carrying its moments table, **a register row**,
+   **whichever lifecycle pieces it actually needs**, and — if it accumulates — **a stated
+   contraction**. → *The mechanism directory*, *Moments*.
+
+   **Which lifecycle pieces, and each absence is declared rather than silent:**
+
+   | it has | when | when absent |
+   |---|---|---|
+   | `<slug>.rules.md` | it injects rules into instruction files it did not write | it injects none |
+   | `<slug>.install.js` / `.uninstall.js` | it has touchpoints that are **not** injected rules — a `settings.json` entry, a directory, a registration | injected rules are its only touchpoints; `inject-rules.js` is then the whole lifecycle |
+   | `<slug>.extract.js` | a clean copy takes some of its paths | a clean copy takes none — say which, and why, in the doc |
+   | `<slug>.announces.md` | its hooks place blocks in a session's context — the table declares each announcement's name, part module, event, **quiet condition** and the records it **watches**, and the part answers the runner through the `{name, body, message}` contract instead of writing stdout (definition: M00's doc; runner, ledger and staleness: M03's) | its hooks never speak, declared in the file as `none` so absence stays distinguishable from forgot |
+   | `<slug>.maintain.js` | its records have a checkable contract — then they are maintained by script, never by a session reading them. Check mode in the suite; fix mode on pickup; **format never content, live rows only**, archived history exempt *(0059, the operator, 2026-08-29)* | its records take judgment, or it has none |
+
+   **Some mechanisms are always on** and take none of the three: nothing can install or
+   uninstall the thing that defines what installing means. Say so in the register row.
+
+   - **Whether `install.js` earns its existence at all is still open** →
+     [0044.0220](../../../docs/tickets/0044.0220-mechanism-shape-lifecycle.md). A clean copy
+     copies files rather than running installers, so its only reader may be a person already
+     reading the doc. **Narrowed 2026-08-28**: two classes now legitimately have none, so the
+     question is no longer *does any mechanism need one* but *does the remaining class*.
+8. **Keep the instruction surface to instructions and compact examples.** Allowlist;
+   everything else goes to the sidecar.
+   - **A count is derived or it is not stated.** Point at the list; let the reader
+     count `[E11]`.
+
+     <!-- BEGIN INJECTED staggered-refiling -->
+     **Owned by `staggered-refiling`. Do not edit this block here** — it is written by `inject-rules.js` from that mechanism's rules file, and an edit made here is not kept — the next install overwrites it, printing what it took. Change it in [its doc](../../../mechanisms/staggered-refiling/staggered-refiling.doc.md).
+
+     **Log the occasion either way** — this rule is rule A of the staggered-refiling trial,
+     and a clean occasion is a datum, not a non-event:
+     `node experiments/lib/experiment-record.js staggered-refiling occasion-a <followed|ignored> "…"`.
+     <!-- END INJECTED staggered-refiling -->
+   - A rule states its **strength** and **who may change it**, inline.
+   - Its evidence is **cited by id**, not restated: `[E1]`, `[E2]`, allocated in order and
+     **never reused** — a recycled id resolves silently to the wrong entry. Bare id within
+     its own sidecar, qualified outside it. A cited id resolving to nothing is a defect; an
+     entry nothing cites is not.
+9. **Name what retires it** — refuted, superseded, subsumed, purpose gone. **A cap is not a
+   removal condition**: it says when something must go, never which thing.
+10. **Name what will grade it, and it is not you.** Pre-register what would show it working,
+   in a form a later party can answer without asking what you meant.
+
+## Amend
+
+1. **Derive the reach; never remember it.** Enumerate from the source that already knows.
+   Recall finds the site you came for and stops, and a comment left at that site is a note
+   next to one of the places. If the reach cannot be derived, say so — the coupling has moved
+   rather than gone.
+2. **Every reliance, not the one that sent you**: prose describing it, checks assuming it,
+   contracts specifying it. **What the change makes stale is part of the change**, not
+   follow-up.
+3. **Re-check the seam, both ends.** An amendment can satisfy the end you are holding and
+   break the other. If no seam was named, name it now.
+4. **Reviewing one nothing disturbed** — are both ends still there, has it ever been watched
+   failing, does its retirement condition still describe anything, has what it was built
+   against moved. **Quiet is not evidence it works**: a guard on a rare irreversible act is
+   silent by design, and low traffic is the signature of what must never be removed. Conclude
+   *sound*, *unsound and here is the amendment*, or *cannot tell from here, and this would
+   tell*.
+
+   <!-- BEGIN INJECTED maintenance -->
+   **Owned by `maintenance`. Do not edit this block here** — it is written by `inject-rules.js` from that mechanism's rules file, and an edit made here is not kept — the next install overwrites it, printing what it took. Change it in [its doc](../../../mechanisms/maintenance/maintenance.doc.md).
+
+   **A mechanism reported due is `/maintain`'s** (the operator, 2026-08-30) — that skill holds how
+   to maintain one at every level, and this is a pointer to it rather than a copy of it. A
+   maintenance **is** an amend, so it returns here for the mechanics; what it does not take from
+   here is which level, how far the cascade runs, or what repair means.
+   
+   **Every amend closes the same way** (the operator, 2026-08-29): amending a mechanism ends
+   with `maintenance-mark.js <slug> rules` — the amend just reviewed those rules, so the mark
+   is honest, and it is how marks come to exist at all. A mechanism nobody has amended or
+   maintained carries no mark, produces no dueness, and is caught only by the never-maintained
+   backlog.
+   <!-- END INJECTED maintenance -->
+
+---
+
+**Siblings, by what the reading is for.** `/denoise` reduces what is said twice and trims
+prose to its current state. `/triage`'s sweep asks whether a region still earns its keep, and
+proposes rather than cuts. This skill asks whether a mechanism is **sound and covered at both
+ends**, and repairs what it finds.
+
+<project-local>
+**Layers:** `core/README.md`. The lists four consumers agree on are `.agents/lib/code-roots.js`
+and `.agents/lib/layers.js` — read them rather than deciding a layer by eye, and add to them
+rather than beside them. The enumeration of mechanisms is `mechanisms/mechanism-shape/mechanism-shape.register.md`; incepting one
+adds **a table row and an entry**, the entry appended after the last one and never inside it.
+The row's `doc` column holds the doc's **path**, not a tick — `mechanisms-shape.js` reads it.
+
+**A write that reports success and changes nothing is a failure**, named at the turn boundary
+and registered before it is retried (`/failure`).
+
+**Watched failing means the suite.** `node .claude/hooks/hooks.test.js` — a hook needs a check
+*titled* for it, a script or library needs a call site. Coverage of a file is not coverage of
+what it emits: assert the property, not the presence.
+
+**Where a new part goes** — `code-roots.js` holds the split:
+
+| kind | home | why |
+|---|---|---|
+| hook | `.claude/hooks/`, or `<layer>/hooks/` | speaks the harness's event protocol |
+| CLI the agent runs by path | `.agents/scripts/` | harness-neutral |
+| library | `.agents/lib/` **only if hooks and scripts both use it** | a hook-only library stays with the hooks |
+| doc, install, uninstall, extract, evidence | `mechanisms/<slug>/` | lifecycle and story, not working parts |
+
+**Incepting a hook, concretely:**
+
+1. **Register it** in `.claude/settings.json` — `SessionStart`, `PreToolUse` with a `matcher`,
+   `PostToolUse`, `PostToolUseFailure`, or `SessionEnd`. Unregistered, it is dead code that
+   tests green.
+2. **Beat once each way.** `require('./beat')('<name>', 'enter')` at the top, and exactly one
+   exit, from `process.on('exit', …)`. Never beat at a terminal branch as well — that writes
+   two exits per enter ([0016](../../../docs/tickets/0016-hook-liveness.md)).
+3. **Catch everything.** A hook must never break the turn it observes.
+4. **Take an argv override** for the file or root it reads, so both polarities run against a
+   fixture; kind-check it with `.agents/lib/argv-path.js`, because a wrong-kind path must not
+   produce the same silence as success. **Put the fixture where the hook's own scope test
+   accepts it**, or it declines the file and the asserted silence is unearned.
+5. **Warn, unless a person set the rule and the match is exact.** A guard that refuses on a
+   heuristic gets routed around.
+6. **Run it by hand only as** `LIFE_HOOKS_LOG=<path> node .claude/hooks/<hook>.js` — otherwise
+   the beat forges a wake, and `guard-beat-forge` will stop you.
+
+**Deriving the reach, concretely:** `code-roots.js` and `layers.js` for paths,
+`readers-named.js` for instrument outputs with no mechanical reader, `links-resolve.js` for
+citations that stopped resolving, `.agents/scripts/repair-citations.js` and `close-ticket.js`
+for a move. Prefer one of these to a grep composed from memory; where none fits, write the
+enumeration into the check rather than into the commit message.
+
+**Grading is `/ticket`'s field and a later session's act** — meta-rule 6, and
+`grading-due.js` announces what is owed. Committing is `/commit`'s and needs no permission.
+
+**When something goes wrong while building, `/failure` owns it**, and an occurrence touching
+an open ticket is struck: `node .agents/lib/strike.js <ticket-slug> "<one line>"`.
+
+**Expansion has a register:** [0028](../../../docs/tickets/0028-reasoning-failure-class.md),
+whose *class* question is **deferred by the operator** pending their own reading. Using the
+shape here is prophylaxis at build time and settles nothing about that deferral.
+
+**`/implement` and `/sync-arch` are not this skill and are not superseded by it** — software
+delivery skills held for a codebase this repo does not have. Do not merge them in, and do not
+route corpus work to them.
+</project-local>

