+# reasoning — evidence
+
+Why this skill has the shape it has. The skill states what is true; this holds how it got
+there, what it cost, and what has been refuted. Reached from `SKILL.md`, never in ordinary
+work.
+
+The mechanism doc is `mechanisms/reasoning/reasoning.doc.md` (M22, → 0044.0230). This sidecar
+is the skill's story; the specimens themselves are `memory/reasoning.md`.
+
+## E1 — the description glossed the kinds, and the gloss had drifted
+
+*2026-08-29, the operator: expand the description to name the kinds.*
+
+The description read *a scope confused, a category invented that cannot be instantiated, a
+claim asserted from a description instead of the thing, one property read as another* — four
+glosses standing in for a four-row table.
+
+Two of the four named nothing in the table. *A scope confused* and *a category invented that
+cannot be instantiated* are 0028's origin specimens, not kinds, and they had survived into the
+description as if they were. Meanwhile **both `unexpanded-*` kinds were absent** — the pair the
+skill's own body calls *that ticket's named shape*, and the two that most specimens land in.
+
+So the one surface forced into every session carried a vocabulary that did not match the one
+the skill actually uses, and nothing could catch it: a gloss and a table cannot be diffed.
+
+**Naming the slugs is shorter than glossing them**, so the tier-1 measurement did not move —
+23 skill descriptions, 1578 tokens, against `CLAUDE.md`'s 1974. The change 0046 warns about
+(descriptions as unpriced tier-1 growth) does not apply to a swap that shortens.
+
+**The seam this closes:** the description is the only part of a skill a session sees without
+invoking it. A vocabulary a session cannot see is one it cannot use, and this specimen is a
+session inventing a term while a five-row table sat one file away.
+
+## E2 — `jargon-not-glossary`, and why it is mechanical rather than stylistic
+
+*2026-08-29, the operator, from a specimen in `memory/reasoning.md` the same day.*
+
+A session coined *abstraction over a family* to warn against general theories built over
+specific defects — while `core/glossary.md`'s `Meta-mechanism` entry already carried
+`_Avoid_: framework, meta-layer, governance`, and the operator's own plain phrasing of the
+same hazard was in `docs/concerns.md` and was quoted back to them one paragraph later.
+
+The kind is not *use plain words*. It is that **a coinage cannot be checked.** A glossary
+governs the words it knows; an invented term is neither the governed word nor on any
+avoid-list, so every instrument the tree has for this is routed around at once. That makes it
+a detection problem rather than a taste problem, which is why it earns a kind.
+
+It is the fifth kind and the first added since the four were drafted. Whether it stands,
+merges or renames is [0028](../../../docs/tickets/0028-reasoning-failure-class.md)'s, which the
+operator has deferred until they have read on the subject; adding it now is theirs to do and
+not a session's.

