+---
+name: ticket
+description: >-
+  Decompose work into independently-completable tickets and register them on the queue in
+  the same pass. Use to mint a ticket — possibly a single one — for anything that will
+  outlive the session that noticed it; to grade a built one against its artifacts, when
+  this session built none of it; and to close one whose criteria have been graded.
+---
+
+# Decompose into tickets
+
+Break work into independently-grabbable slices, written as markdown under
+`docs/tickets/`. The parent is a concern at inception, a coarse ticket when zooming in,
+or the chunk under discussion; the same slicing applies at every resolution.
+
+The shape of a ticket, its naming, and the queue are
+[TICKET-FORMAT.md](./TICKET-FORMAT.md)'s. Read it before writing one; restate none of it.
+
+## A ticket struck again records the strike
+
+Where the work you are doing shows an existing ticket costing something again — a defect it
+would have prevented, a decision it is blocking — log one line before anything else:
+
+```bash
+node .agents/lib/strike.js <ticket-slug> "one line"
+```
+
+It increments `- **Strikes:** N` on the ticket. `/triage` ranks by *what recurrence would
+cost*; without this that term is estimated by the session doing the ranking, and with it, it
+is counted. Slug, never number. Read at wake by `queue-next.js`.
+→ [EVIDENCE.md](./EVIDENCE.md)
+
+## Why a ticket rather than a note
+
+A concern records that something is unresolved. A ticket carries what would resolve it —
+the criteria, the dependency, and the bar for closing. An open question with no ticket
+is a question nobody has decided how to answer, which is the state most of them stay in.
+
+Mint one for anything that will outlive the session. A session that ends is a session
+whose intentions evaporate.
+
+## Process
+
+### 1. Locate the parent
+
+Ask for the parent's path unless it is clear from context. Read it if it is not already
+in context. When the parent is the chunk under discussion there is no file — the ticket
+must then carry its own context.
+
+### 2. Draft slices
+
+Each slice is independently completable and verifiable on its own. Prefer many thin
+slices over few thick ones. A chunk already ticket-sized yields a single ticket — a
+valid outcome, not a failed decomposition.
+
+Mark each **AFK** or **HITL** honestly. This repo runs unattended daily, so the mark is
+the autonomy boundary rather than a note about convenience: AFK means the cron may close
+it alone. A slice whose closing needs a judgment the evidence cannot supply is HITL, and
+saying so is the whole value of the field.
+
+A slice blocked on an unresolved decision begins as a **decision-bearing HITL ticket**.
+It is the eventual work in an earlier phase, not a separate decision slice; name it for
+the outcome it will deliver.
+
+### 3. Quiz
+
+Present the breakdown as a numbered list — title, type, depends on, what of the parent it
+covers. Ask whether the granularity and dependencies are right, whether anything should
+merge or split, and whether the AFK/HITL marks are honest. Iterate until approved.
+
+**Quiz only what is genuinely forked.** Where the decomposition is uncontroversial, register
+it and report rather than asking — attended or not. Someone being available to answer is not
+a reason to spend their attention, and having a recommendation you expect to be taken is the
+tell that there was no fork. Never flip a HITL mark to clear a stall.
+
+### 4. Write and register
+
+Create in dependency order so `Depends on` can reference real filenames. A completed
+blocker lives in `done/` — reference it there. Update the queue in the same pass; a
+ticket that exists only as a file is not on the queue.
+
+### 5. Grading
+
+The act, its bar, and the field it writes are [TICKET-FORMAT.md](./TICKET-FORMAT.md)'s
+*Grading — the act*; this step restates none of it. The moment is a session holding a
+built ticket it did not build — read each criterion against the artifact, not the ticket's
+account of it. `grading-due.js` names what is owed, at `/conclude`.
+
+### 6. Completing
+
+When every box is checked, close through `node .agents/scripts/close-ticket.js <slug>`
+(`--dry` first) — it moves the file to `docs/tickets/done/`, repairs the citations that
+pointed at it, and leaves frozen records dangling by design. Never by hand: the by-hand
+road is how a 2026-08-26 session priced nine reference repairs as too expensive and argued
+for leaving a finished ticket in the queue. Do not close or modify the parent — a parent
+completes on its own criteria, never by its children emptying out.
+
+## Altitude
+
+A slice whose criteria cannot be written as observable outcomes is not yet a ticket →
+`/align` first. Prefer a criterion that a check can verify over one a reader must
+remember to verify.
+
+<project-local>
+Concern promotion: **the row leaves `docs/concerns.md` entirely**, as a ticketed failure
+leaves its register *(the operator, 2026-08-30)*. Move the deliberation into the ticket and
+say there which `C<n>` it came from — ids are never reused, so the citation resolves whether
+or not a row still carries it. A concern and a ticket must never hold two copies of the same
+argument.
+</project-local>

