+# Evidence — triage
+
+Why this skill exists, and what would retire each of its statements. The instruction is in
+`SKILL.md`; nothing here is repeated there.
+
+## What licensed it
+
+Created 2026-08-26 under `/align`, with the operator, from a question they asked about
+`memory/failures.md`: *do we have a reader for it, something that actually resolves them, or
+does it just grow indefinitely?*
+
+It grew indefinitely. Measured that morning:
+
+- **14 entries, 0 ever disposed.** The `## Resolved` section had held nothing for the whole
+  life of the file, while `hooks.test.js` covered its parser — a seam specified at one end,
+  in the register that records that class of defect.
+- **4,217 → 30,217 bytes in two days**, 4 → 14 entries. Per-entry size roughly doubled over
+  the same window, median ~1,235 bytes on day one against ~2,600 on day two.
+- **The cost lands on `/audit`**, the one reader that must read the file whole, at ~7,554
+  tokens and rising.
+
+## Three findings that shaped it, in the order they landed
+
+**1. Scrutiny pointed away from the entries claiming to be handled.** `failures-open.js`
+filtered to `action: nothing yet`, so **8 of 14 entries were invisible** — an entry vanished
+the moment it claimed a mechanism, and nothing anywhere verified that the mechanism existed,
+fired, or helped. The hook now counts what is undisposed instead.
+
+**2. `/audit` already declared this job and never did it.** Its input #4 says mine the
+register for *entries whose action is still `nothing yet` while the cost has risen* —
+selection, stated. Its procedure has no step that does it. The first design put the pass in
+`/audit` for that reason.
+
+**3. That design was killed by a compliance measurement**, and this is the one worth
+keeping. `/audit` had run **once in 13 sessions**, against ~1 arrival per session — a queue
+diverging about 13:1. A threshold-driven wake signal aimed at `/audit` was not a hypothesis:
+`lookups-unread.js` had been reporting a standing backlog of 451 rows for days with that
+result. So the trigger moved off `/audit` entirely.
+
+## Why the alarm is on the derivative
+
+A backlog alarm keyed to an absolute threshold only fires once you are already behind, and
+there is no good value for it: at 1 it speaks every wake and trains its reader to skip it,
+at 10 it is late, and nothing between is principled. The operator's question — *why not due
+at 1?* — is what exposed that the threshold was the wrong instrument rather than the wrong
+number.
+
+Growth since the last pass is the signal that is actually news.
+
+## What the dispositions cost, and the bar that was rejected
+
+`done` claims only that the work landed. The stronger bar considered and rejected was
+**observed catch** — the mechanism demonstrably caught a real instance. It was rejected on a
+measurement: across all 14 entries, **23 hooks and 152 checks had caught 0 of them.** Every
+one was caught by inspection (6), another party (7), or a rule read at the moment it applied
+(1). A bar of *observed catch* would have disposed nothing, reproducing the state it was
+meant to fix.
+
+A middle bar — *independent re-proof*, a later session re-running the watched-failing test —
+was also dropped, because routing work out to tickets already puts a different session
+between the claim and its acceptance. It remains the obvious upgrade if `done` turns out to
+be too cheap.
+
+Whether a mechanism sits in the path of live work is
+[0016](../../../docs/tickets/0016-hook-liveness.md)'s question and stays open there.
+
+## Why selection is not execution
+
+Three backlogs, three owners already: `/ticket` mints and closes, `/mechanism` builds and
+amends, `/comment` replies. *(This said `/implement` until 2026-08-27, which was the routing
+half of that skill's defect: it is unported software-delivery and no corpus work ever reached
+it — `mechanism/EVIDENCE.md`.)* A skill that both chose and did the work would be a fourth container
+named for one of its contents — the pattern this repo logged three times in one day
+(`/ticket`, `/comment`, `tier`) and carries an open retrieval miss for.
+
+**Amended 2026-09-02, at the operator's instruction, after a pass demonstrated the gap.**
+Triage pass 51 ranked the queue, named `0015` next, and named no skill to resolve it — the
+body said the work *goes to* an owner and never said the pass *names* one, so a pass could
+satisfy every sentence in the skill and still hand the next session a sorted list. The
+sentence now requires the owner by name, and the operator's framing is the reason: a pass
+should resolve what is due, not only convert things into tickets.
+
+**Then the sentence grew a taxonomy, and the taxonomy was in the wrong file.** Three versions
+in one hour, each ended by an operator catch, and the third is the one that matters. Version
+two added `/maintain` beside `/mechanism`; version three split them by verb after the operator
+asked whether `/maintain` owns amendment — it does, and that skill's own second line says so:
+*a maintenance **is** an amend — that skill holds the mechanics, this one holds the order.*
+Version four deleted the whole distinction from this file, at the operator's instruction:
+**triage should redirect to `/implement` rather than elaborate on the amending skills, because
+`/implement` carries verification rules a pass does not have.**
+
+That is the correct cut and the first three versions were the same error at increasing
+resolution — a pass that sorts owners is a second home for a boundary two other skills already
+define, and it hands work on carrying none of the checks the owner would have applied. The
+routing question moved to `/implement`'s first act, where it is a build's own first decision;
+this file now names one owner for work and stops.
+
+**What the discarded versions were right about**, kept because the reasoning survives the
+wording: `/maintain`'s absence from this file *was* a one-ended seam (meta-rule 2). The
+maintenance mechanism's injected block has said since 2026-08-29 that dueness is a backlog
+input and *a picked row goes to `/maintain`* — the producing end — while the body named three
+owners and not that one. Seven maintenance rows were due the day this was written and no pass
+had ever picked one. The block still carries that routing and is the right home for it, which
+is why the body no longer needs to.
+
+**`/implement` stayed out for one hour, then came back, and both halves belong on the record.**
+It was dropped from this sentence on 2026-08-27 as unported reference-corpus software delivery.
+Re-read 2026-09-02 rather than inherited: still zero project adaptation, still named by no
+session record, still routing to a `/tdd` this tree does not have, so it stayed out and the
+stale half was called as `core/process.md`, whose stage 4 kept routing every build to it.
+
+**That reading was overtaken the same hour, by the operator authorising the rewrite it
+assumed was not available.** The skill was rewritten for this tree — the boundary question
+first, the criteria as the contract, no grading by the builder — and rejoins the sentence as a
+real owner. What the hour bought is worth keeping: the decision to exclude it was correct
+while the file was what it was, and *unported* was a fact about a file rather than a verdict
+on a name. `C38` carries the measurement that made the rewrite necessary and stays raised for
+a later pass to dispose, since this session wrote it.
+
+The same reasoning kept the name `triage` honest: [0022](../../../docs/tickets/0022-inbox-triage.md)
+already called the inbox problem *triage*, so the inbox was admitted as a client of this
+skill rather than left as a competing build.
+
+## Why the sweep exists, and why it is bounded the way it is
+
+Asked for by the operator, 2026-08-27: triage should occasionally read the standing corpus
+for what can be optimised, generalised, simplified or dropped without losing functionality.
+
+**The gap it fills is structural.** Every backlog this skill reads is fed by something going
+wrong — a failure, a concern, an inbox item, a ticket minted from one of those. A mechanism
+that works produces no entry anywhere, so it is never looked at again, and a mechanism that
+has been superseded or duplicated is indistinguishable from one that is load-bearing. An
+outside reading of the whole tree the same day named the general form: this corpus is
+excellent at learning from failure and has no route that reaches what merely persists.
+
+**Census, not framework, is the operator's own constraint** and predates the ask —
+`docs/concerns.md`, 2026-08-26: *the corpus has ~5 mechanism families and no census of them
+… wanted: a census that reports unevenness, **not a framework** — every failure recorded
+here is specific, and an abstraction hides an instance's bug better than it prevents it.*
+The bar in the body is that sentence made operational.
+
+**Two instances before generalising** comes from the same place. Six of this repo's tickets
+were already about shape rather than about a feature when that concern was written, which is
+abstraction pressure showing up scattered — and a sweep licensed to propose abstractions
+would be a seventh source of it.
+
+**Quiet is not evidence of useless** is the sharpest of the bars and the one most likely to
+be violated by a session in a hurry. The measurement behind it: of twelve registered
+failures, five were caught outside the session and **zero** by any of twenty-three hooks —
+and the hooks with no catches include the two strict-rule guards, whose subject is
+irreversible acts that have not yet been attempted. Activity is the wrong axis entirely, and
+a sweep ranking by it would delete the guards first.
+
+**Proposes, never cuts** is meta-rule 6 applied where it matters most. Removal is the only
+disposition that cannot be undone by noticing later, so the session that spots a candidate
+must not be the session that grades its removal.
+
+**Prose is in scope, and the seam moved once during the same conversation.** The first
+version drew the line at mechanism-against-prose and handed prose findings to `/denoise`
+untouched. The operator's correction: *compaction of redundant verbatim is a triage finding
+too — the entire denoise practice can be integrated into triage, on occasion.* They are
+right, and the reason is that both are the same act on different substrates.
+
+What the correction does **not** license is copying `/denoise`'s rules into this skill. That
+would be a second home for dedup, the pointer form and the evolution-trim, which is the
+defect the practice itself exists to remove. So the sweep covers prose by **invoking**
+`/denoise`, and what it supplies is the one thing that skill has never had: an occasion.
+`/denoise` runs on request, and nothing in this tree has ever created the request.
+
+`compact` is a named finding rather than a flavour of `duplicate` because it carries a
+condition the others do not — the pre-merge text is archived, so the merge is reversible.
+That rule is `core/README.md`'s, under eviction, and ticket
+[0100](../../../docs/tickets/0100-compaction-and-the-unit.md) owns the open half of it.
+A merge nobody can unmake is a deletion that has not admitted it, and deletion is the one
+disposition a later reader cannot correct.
+
+## Two additions on 2026-09-02, and one is a rule this skill only points at
+
+**A pass may not elect its own rows.** The eligibility rule already said a session may not
+dispose what it wrote; the ranked backlog needed the same sentence, because *Ordered* removes
+nothing and so looked exempt. Passes 55 and 56 both hit it: every ticket minted that day was
+the ranking session's, one of them would very likely have taken the front on the cost test, and
+neither pass could elect it. Saying so is the point — the front was then held by default rather
+than by argument, and the next pass needs to know which.
+
+**The `ticketed` exception is `/failure`'s and is referenced, not restated.** It changes what a
+pass *finds* rather than what a pass may *do*: entries already carried by a ticket leave without
+waiting, so a register holds closer to what still wants a decision. Its reasoning and the
+measurements behind it live in that skill's `EVIDENCE.md`.
+
+## The hand-on, 2026-09-03
+
+**Twenty picks, zero hand-ons, two sessions.** Passes 59–68 (session 0042) and 69–78 (session
+0043) each picked a due mechanism, wrote *owner `/maintain`* into the queue's record, and moved
+to the next pass. Both sessions read *a pass selects and does not maintain* as a ban on the
+session rather than a bound on the pass, while the body's own sentence — *hands the work itself
+to the skill it names* — sat above it. Session 0042's record filed *whether `/maintain` should run
+inside a pass* as a question with no home. The operator, on being asked why triage does not
+maintain and hearing the misreading restated: *"'goes to maintain' means triage should use
+maintain or other skills to fix!!!"* — then, on the design: keep triage as selection, no separate
+fix skill; `/implement` is already the router for a picked ticket, and what was missing was the
+sentence at the close. That sentence is the *Then hand on* paragraph. Specimens:
+`memory/reasoning.md` 2026-09-03 (`unexpanded-lives`), `memory/failures.md` 2026-09-03, strike 3
+on [0059](../../../docs/tickets/0059-a-mechanism-is-rechecked-when-what-governs-it-moves.md).
+
+The seam this closes was one-ended: the pick named its consumer and nothing named the moment
+the consumer runs. The daily loop had it — `core/process.md` stage 4, *work the queue in its own
+order* — and an attended session asked for passes did not, which is why the count grew only on
+days a person asked for many passes at once.
+
+## What would retire the statements
+
+- **The hand-on** — a run of passes whose hand-ons are each abandoned part-way because the
+  work was an afternoon and the session had nine more passes to run, which would mean the
+  bound belongs on the number of passes a session takes rather than on what a pass does; or an
+  operator instruction that is routinely *selection only*, which would mean the default was set
+  the wrong way round.
+
+- ~~**The quota of one** — a pass that reliably disposes more than one without being skipped.
