+  for is unrefuted rather than disproved, which is why the replacement keeps *one per backlog,
+  never two*. What retires the new shape: a pass that gets skipped for its size, or a backlog
+  routinely reported unadvanced for the same reason twice running, which would mean the
+  eligibility escape is carrying work the rule should have priced.
+- **Cost-ranking over age** — a run of picks where the cost ranking and the age ranking agree,
+  which would mean the ranking is doing no work.
+- **Order within a backlog only** — a session that needs to choose between two backlogs and
+  finds `core/process.md` silent on it.
+- **The whole skill** — a backlog that shrinks across passes with nobody running triage.
+- **The inward sweep** — a run of sweeps whose findings are all declined at grading, which
+  would mean the bar admits taste; or a sweep finding that turns out to have removed
+  something load-bearing, which would mean *proposes, never cuts* was not enough separation.
+- **Two instances before generalising** — a single-instance finding that a later session
+  shows was worth generalising on sight, with the second instance arriving afterwards.
+- **Naming the resolving skill** — a run of passes where the named owner is always the one a
+  reader would have guessed from the item, which would mean the sentence buys nothing; or a
+  pass that cannot name one, which would mean the owner set is incomplete rather than the
+  pass careless. **The second half fired the hour it was written**, before any pass used it,
